@{ Layout = null; }
<html>
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" name="viewport" />
    <title>Security Code FAQS</title>
    @StaticResources.AssetStyles.RenderCommonWithDarkMode("/bundles/common/common")
    <link href="~/assets/styles/security/lean-more.min.css" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" />
</head>
<body>
    <h1 class="page-title">Security Code FAQS</h1>
    <div class="content">
        <ol class="list-faqs">
            <li>
                <strong>What is Security Code?</strong>
                <p>
                    It is 6 numeric digits [0-9] and you will be asked to enter this security code each time you log-in for additional authentication.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>How to setup security code?</strong>
                <div>
                    <p>Input the security code and confirm it, follow the notes below.</p>
                    <div class="italic">Note:</div>
                    <ul class="setup">
                        <li>
                            Security code must be 6 numeric digits [0-9] and contains at
                            least 2 different digits.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Security code must not a ‘Forward Run or ‘Backward Run’ number
                            ( A ‘Forward Run’ number is an integer whose digits are all in consecutive, ascending
                            order, left to right; whereas a ‘Backward Run’ number is an interger whose digits are all in
                            consecutive, descending order, left to right. For example: 123456, 456789, 764321, etc.. are
                            not allowed.)
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Does the security code expire?</strong>
                <p>
                    It is not expired but you should change it periodically.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>What happens if I entered wrong security code?</strong>
                <p>
                    It will require you to re-enter security code again, be noted that your account
                    will be closed after entering the wrong security code over 5 times. Please contact your upline or
                    CSD in this case.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>What if I have forgotten my security code?</strong>
                <p>
                    Contact your upline or CSD to reset your security code.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>How do I change my security code?</strong>
                <p>
                    At the Home page, go to Security tab, then choose Security Code link, then change your security code.
                </p>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</body>
</html>